module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Unramified.Differentials
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.SheafOfDifferentialsFiniteType
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.UniversalDerivationVanishing
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# The vanishing of a sheaf of differentials read on Kähler differentials of charts

Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a morphism of algebraic spaces over a scheme `S`.  Its sheaf of
differentials `Ω_{X/Y}` of Stacks 04CT is by construction the sheafification of the presheaf of
sectionwise Kähler differentials of `f♯ : f⁻¹𝒪_Y ⟶ 𝒪_X`, whose value at an étale chart `W` of
`X` is the module of Kähler differentials of the ring map `(f⁻¹𝒪_Y)(W) ⟶ 𝒪_X(W)`.

`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isZero_sheafOfDifferentials_iff` expresses the vanishing of `Ω_{X/Y}`
as the vanishing of the universal derivation on the sections of the *sheaf*.  What is added here
is the translation of that into a statement about those Kähler differentials themselves: the
unit of the sheafification is not only locally surjective but locally *bijective*, so a section
of the presheaf which the unit kills already dies on a covering sieve.  Since the unit carries
the sectionwise Kähler differential of a regular function to its universal differential, this
says that `Ω_{X/Y}` vanishes exactly when every regular function on every étale chart has, on a
covering sieve of that chart, a vanishing Kähler differential.

This is the form in which the vanishing of `Ω_{X/Y}` bears on a *scheme-level* sheaf of
differentials: the sections of the scheme-level sheaf over an affine open lying over an affine
open of the base are Kähler differentials of an honest map of rings (Stacks 01UT), whereas the
sections of `Ω_{X/Y}` over a chart are not given by any formula.

On the scheme side the corresponding translation is an equality, not a local one: by Stacks 01UT
the sections of the sheaf of relative differentials of a morphism of schemes over an affine open
lying over an affine open of the base *are* the Kähler differentials of the induced map of rings
of functions, so that sheaf is a zero object exactly when all of those vanish.  One direction of
that is recorded here too; it is the shape in which a scheme-level vanishing is produced from
chart data.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isZero_sheafOfDifferentials_iff_locally_kaehlerDifferential_eq_zero`:
  `Ω_{X/Y}` is a zero object exactly when the Kähler differential of every regular function on
  every étale chart of `X` vanishes on a covering sieve of that chart.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.isZero_relativeDifferentials_of_subsingleton_kaehlerDifferential`:
  a morphism of schemes whose Kähler differentials vanish on every pair of affine charts has a
  zero sheaf of relative differentials.  This is the converse of the sectionwise consequence of
  Stacks 01UT that `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.subsingleton_kaehlerDifferential_resLE` proves.

## Implementation notes

The local bijectivity of the unit is read off the same instance
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smallEtaleRingedSite_wEqualsLocallyBijective` that
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_sieve_mem_span_universalDerivation` uses for the local
surjectivity half, through `CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.W_toSheafify` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.toPresheaf_differentialsSheafifyUnit`, which identifies the underlying
morphism of presheaves of abelian groups of the unit with `CategoryTheory.toSheafify`.  The
covering sieve produced is `CategoryTheory.Presheaf.equalizerSieve` of the Kähler differential
and zero.

In the converse direction the sieve is consumed by the separatedness of `Ω_{X/Y}`, which is a
sheaf: a section whose restrictions along a covering sieve all vanish is zero.

## What is not proved here

This does **not** close the gap of Stacks 04CS in the direction that a vanishing spaces-level
`Ω` forces a scheme-level one to vanish; see the "What is not proved here" section of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/SheafOfDifferentialsSchemeVanishing.lean`.  Two steps
remain between the statement below and such a conclusion, and neither is available:

* the Kähler differentials appearing here are taken relative to the ring `(f⁻¹𝒪_Y)(W)` of
  sections of the inverse image of `𝒪_Y`, which is larger than the ring of functions pulled back
  from a single étale chart of `Y`, so the module appearing here is a *quotient* of the Kähler
  differentials relative to that chart and its vanishing is weaker; closing that step needs that
  the inverse image structure ring is, on a covering sieve, generated by the functions pulled
  back along one chart;
* the covering sieve has to be descended through, which for Kähler differentials needs their
  étale base change together with the faithful flatness of an étale covering.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 04CT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04CT), the sheaf of
  differentials of a morphism of algebraic spaces and its universal derivation.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04CS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04CS), the comparison of the
  small Zariski and small étale differentials of a morphism of schemes.
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

/-- **A morphism of schemes whose Kähler differentials vanish on every pair of affine charts has
a zero sheaf of relative differentials.**  Formal unramifiedness of a morphism of schemes is, by
definition, formal unramifiedness of the induced map of rings of functions on every affine open
of the source lying over an affine open of the target, which for a ring map is the vanishing of
its Kähler differentials; and a formally unramified morphism has a zero sheaf of relative
differentials by Stacks 02H9.

This is the converse of the consequence of Stacks 01UT that
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.subsingleton_kaehlerDifferential_resLE` proves, and it is the shape in
which a scheme-level vanishing is produced from data on affine charts. -/
@[ega "IV 17.4.2" "a) ⇒ c)"]
theorem isZero_relativeDifferentials_of_subsingleton_kaehlerDifferential
    {X T : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ T)
    (h : ∀ {V : T.Opens}, IsAffineOpen V → ∀ {U : X.Opens}, IsAffineOpen U →
      ∀ hUV : U ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V,
        Subsingleton (CommRingCat.KaehlerDifferential (f.appLE V U hUV))) :
    IsZero (relativeDifferentials f) := by
  refine (formallyUnramified_iff_isZero_relativeDifferentials f).mp
    ⟨fun {V} hV {U} hU hUV ↦ ?_⟩
  let : Algebra Γ(T, V) Γ(X, U) := (f.appLE V U hUV).hom.toAlgebra
  rw [show (f.appLE V U hUV).hom = algebraMap Γ(T, V) Γ(X, U) from rfl,
    RingHom.formallyUnramified_algebraMap, Algebra.formallyUnramified_iff]
  exact h hV hU hUV

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
variable {X Y : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS}

/-- The unit of the sheafification presenting `Ω_{X/Y}` is locally injective: it is a local
equivalence of presheaves of abelian groups, and on the small étale site of an algebraic space
those are exactly the locally bijective morphisms. -/
theorem isLocallyInjective_differentialsSheafifyUnit (f : X ⟶ Y) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).J
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf
          ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
            (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).O)).obj).map
        (differentialsSheafifyUnit B S hS f)) := by
  rw [toPresheaf_differentialsSheafifyUnit B S hS f]
  exact ((smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).J.W_toSheafify (A := AddCommGrpCat.{u})
    (PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.DifferentialsConstruction.relativeDifferentials'
      (structureSharpInverseImage B S hS f).hom).presheaf).isLocallyInjective

/-- **The vanishing of `Ω_{X/Y}` is the local vanishing of the Kähler differentials of the chart
rings.**  The sheaf of differentials of a morphism `f : X ⟶ Y` of algebraic spaces over `S` is a
zero object exactly when, for every étale chart `W` of `X` and every regular function `c` on
`W`, there is a covering sieve of `W` on whose members the Kähler differential of the
restriction of `c` vanishes.

`Ω_{X/Y}` is the sheafification of the presheaf of sectionwise Kähler differentials of
`f♯ : f⁻¹𝒪_Y ⟶ 𝒪_X`, and the unit of that sheafification is locally bijective.  In the forward
direction the universal derivation vanishes by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isZero_sheafOfDifferentials_iff`, so the unit kills the sectionwise
Kähler differential of `c`, and local injectivity produces the sieve.  In the converse direction
the restrictions of the universal differential of `c` along the sieve vanish, and `Ω_{X/Y}`
being a sheaf is separated, so that universal differential vanishes. -/
theorem isZero_sheafOfDifferentials_iff_locally_kaehlerDifferential_eq_zero (f : X ⟶ Y) :
    IsZero (sheafOfDifferentials B S hS f) ↔
      ∀ (W : SmallEtale B S hS X.1) (c : chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 W),
        ∃ T : Sieve W, T ∈ (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).J W ∧
          ∀ ⦃Bo : SmallEtale B S hS X.1⦄ (g : Bo ⟶ W), T.arrows g →
            CommRingCat.KaehlerDifferential.d
                (f := (structureSharpInverseImage B S hS f).hom.app (op Bo))
                (chartRestrict (hF := X.2) g c) = 0 := by
  constructor
  · intro hzero W c
    have hunit : ((differentialsSheafifyUnit B S hS f).app (op W)).hom
          (CommRingCat.KaehlerDifferential.d
            (f := (structureSharpInverseImage B S hS f).hom.app (op W)) c) =
        ((differentialsSheafifyUnit B S hS f).app (op W)).hom 0 :=
      (differentialsSheafifyUnit_app_d B S hS f W c).trans
        (((isZero_sheafOfDifferentials_iff B S hS f).mp hzero (op W) c).trans (map_zero _).symm)
    refine ⟨_, (isLocallyInjective_differentialsSheafifyUnit B S hS f).equalizerSieve_mem
      _ _ hunit, fun Bo g hg ↦ ?_⟩
    have hg' : ((PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.DifferentialsConstruction.relativeDifferentials'
            (structureSharpInverseImage B S hS f).hom).map g.op).hom
          (CommRingCat.KaehlerDifferential.d
            (f := (structureSharpInverseImage B S hS f).hom.app (op W)) c) =
        ((PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.DifferentialsConstruction.relativeDifferentials'
            (structureSharpInverseImage B S hS f).hom).map g.op).hom 0 := hg
    rw [map_zero] at hg'
    exact (PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.DifferentialsConstruction.relativeDifferentials'_map_d
      (structureSharpInverseImage B S hS f).hom g.op c).symm.trans hg'
  · intro hloc
    refine (isZero_sheafOfDifferentials_iff B S hS f).mpr ?_
    rintro ⟨W⟩ c
    obtain ⟨T, hT, hTzero⟩ := hloc W c
    refine (sheafOfDifferentials B S hS f).isSheaf.isSeparated _ _ hT
      ((universalDerivation B S hS f).d c) 0 fun Bo g hg ↦ ?_
    refine Eq.trans ?_ (map_zero _).symm
    have hzc : (universalDerivation B S hS f).d (chartRestrict (hF := X.2) g c) = 0 := by
      rw [← differentialsSheafifyUnit_app_d B S hS f Bo (chartRestrict (hF := X.2) g c),
        hTzero g hg]
      exact map_zero _
    exact ((universalDerivation B S hS f).d_map g.op c).symm.trans hzc

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
